Playing cautiously and patiently has paid off for Qwyeth the Valkyrie
thus far.  Early on, my dog led most of the charge to Minetown, which,
combined with the clearing out of two shopkeepers' stores, allowed me
to donate enough gold for 9 points of divine protection at XL2.  This
and the various pieces of armor obtained in the mines added up to a
-17 AC, which made clearing out the rest of the mines quite easy.

After emptying the wine cellar of loot and hauling every single item
of interest back to the minetown altar, I set to the tedious task of
identifying everything.  The RNG has denied me holy water or blessed
identification scrolls, so I made extensive use of pricing in the
general store and nakedness in locked rooms.  Unfortunately, I wound
up hitting that shopkeeper while confused, and my entire stash was
nearby so I had no choice to murder the unforgiving creep.  I found
out the hard way that praying after murder is a sure way to give up
that divine protection, but I had enough armor by that point to get
down to -10 AC, so I pressed on.

I made some mistakes in Sokoban, which required the destruction of two
boulders and nakedly slipping past a third.  I also had to destroy a
cave spider (who had found a nice hiding spot behind a boulder) with a
wand of fire, which bounced back and destroyed about two-thirds of the
potions and scrolls I had with me (as the only bag I'd found yet was a
bag of tricks).  In exchange for that bad luck, I scored the bag of
holding.

I cleared the next several dungeon levels methodically, keeping my
stash by the altar on level 4 (and later hauling the entire darn chest
down to level 7), and encountered a big room for the first time in my
career as a nethacker.  The room was a bit anticlimactic, as it only
contained monsters that I was confident I could melee down with a
minimum of fuss.  After considering my position for a while, I charged
right in and had no real trouble, however my trusty dog died to the
poisoned blade of an A.  I should have realized that a domestic animal
can't be expected to continue to be effective in combat indefinitely.

I ventured several levels beneath that big room and encountered my
quest portal.  This shocked me as a player; I realized then that my
understanding of nethack strategy has become more or less sound and I
may one day actually ascend a character... perhaps, should the favor
of the RNG be upon me, even this one.

So here I am.  I've killed every hostile thing above the big room and
most between it and the quest portal.  My intrinsics include speed and
cold (of course), fire, and poison resistance, telepathy, and
teleportitis (on purpose:  I had a =oTC and it seemed too useful to
pass up).  I've obtained a decent stock of stuff, and my AC is -17
(it'll be -20 if I can manage to foo-proof some of these armor
pieces).  I carry 3 unicorn horns and 4 lizard corpses, and a cursed ?
oT in case things get really hairy.  I have a /oFire for permanent
Elbereth but I don't know how many charges it has.  I do not have any
source of MR, reflection, or wishing, and I'm giving some thought to
going mining in hopes to find enough $ to buy back the protection I
lost early on.  My luck is certainly bad, because I've foolishly kept
my luckstone out since cheating in Sokoban.  I fear my god and
alignment are unhappy as well; ever since killing that shopkeeper I've
been afraid to pray, and I've also gotten in the habit of killing and
eating peaceful Tengu in hopes of no longer having to wear my =oTC.
(5 corpses and still no intrinsic).

I'm in totally unfamiliar territory and I would like to hear what RGRN
has to say before I proceed further.  The rest of my details are
below.  Thanks in advance for all your advice.

